#: ../../../tools/pass_diff.md:1
msgid "Pass Diff"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/pass_diff.md:3
msgid "Superseded — use IR Lower Trace"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/pass_diff.md:6
msgid ""
"This tool has been superseded by **IR Lower Trace** (`TL_LOWER_TRACE`), "
"documented in {doc}`lower_trace`. New users should use IR Lower Trace "
"directly — it provides phase context, codegen capture, multi-run "
"accumulation, and an enhanced HTML report. `TILELANG_PASS_DIFF` is retained "
"only for backward compatibility."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/pass_diff.md:12
msgid ""
"Pass Diff shows how TileLang's TIR changes as compiler passes run. It "
"captures the IR before and after each pass, computes a unified diff, and "
"writes the result to the terminal, an interactive HTML report, or both."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/pass_diff.md:16
msgid ""
"Use the environment-variable workflow to observe the complete lowering "
"pipeline without modifying a program. Use the Python API when you want to "
"apply and inspect a specific pass sequence."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/pass_diff.md:20
msgid "Observe the Lowering Pipeline"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/pass_diff.md:22
msgid "Set `TILELANG_PASS_DIFF` before starting the Python process:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/pass_diff.md:24
msgid ""
"# Print colored diffs while passes run.\n"
"TILELANG_PASS_DIFF=terminal python my_script.py\n"
"\n"
"# Write an HTML report.\n"
"TILELANG_PASS_DIFF=html python my_script.py\n"
"\n"
"# Print terminal diffs and write an HTML report.\n"
"TILELANG_PASS_DIFF=both python my_script.py\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/pass_diff.md:35
msgid ""
"TileLang reads this setting when `tilelang` is imported and installs a "
"process- wide hook around TVM pass execution. Setting the variable after "
"importing TileLang does not enable the hook for that process."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/pass_diff.md:3
msgid "Variable"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/pass_diff.md:3
msgid "Accepted values"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/pass_diff.md:3 ../../../tools/pass_diff.md:64
msgid "Default"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/pass_diff.md:3
msgid "`TILELANG_PASS_DIFF`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/pass_diff.md:3
msgid ""
"`terminal`, `html`, `both`; `1`, `true`, `yes`, and `on` also select "
"terminal output"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/pass_diff.md:3
msgid "`0` (disabled)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/pass_diff.md:3
msgid "`TILELANG_PASS_DIFF_OUTPUT`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/pass_diff.md:3
msgid "Directory for pipeline HTML reports"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/pass_diff.md:3
msgid "`tmp/pass_diff_output`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/pass_diff.md:44
msgid ""
"False-like values (`0`, `false`, `no`, `off`, or an empty string) disable "
"the hook. An unrecognized nonempty value falls back to terminal output."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/pass_diff.md:47
msgid ""
"HTML reports use a timestamped filename such as `pass_diff_20260710_153000."
"html`. The report is refreshed after each pass so a partial result is "
"available even during a long compilation, then finalized at process exit."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/pass_diff.md:52
msgid "Pass Diff HTML report showing TIR before and after a compiler pass"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/pass_diff.md:57
msgid "Pass Diff HTML report."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/pass_diff.md:60
msgid ""
"The HTML viewer provides side-by-side before and after source, collapsible "
"pass sections, expandable unchanged context, copy controls, light and dark "
"themes, and aggregate insertion and deletion counts."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/pass_diff.md:65
msgid ""
"The pipeline hook wraps `tvm.ir.transform.Pass.__call__` for the entire "
"process, so it observes TVM passes outside the immediate `tilelang."
"compile()` call as well. Capturing IR and, in HTML mode, rewriting the "
"report after every pass adds debugging overhead. Leave the feature disabled "
"for normal builds and benchmarks."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/pass_diff.md:71
msgid "Compare Selected Passes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/pass_diff.md:73
msgid ""
"The `pass_diff` Python API accepts a `PrimFunc` or `IRModule` and applies "
"the provided passes in order:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/pass_diff.md:76
msgid ""
"import tilelang\n"
"from tilelang import tvm\n"
"from tilelang.utils.pass_diff import pass_diff\n"
"\n"
"steps = pass_diff(\n"
"    func,\n"
"    [\n"
"        (\"AnnotateDeviceRegions\", tvm.tirx.transform."
"AnnotateDeviceRegions()),\n"
"        (\"SplitHostDevice\", tvm.tirx.transform.SplitHostDevice()),\n"
"        (\"ThreadSync\", tilelang.transform.ThreadSync(\"shared\")),\n"
"    ],\n"
"    mode=\"both\",\n"
"    context=5,\n"
"    html_path=\"tmp/selected_passes.html\",\n"
")\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/pass_diff.md:94
msgid "A single unnamed pass is also accepted:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/pass_diff.md:96
msgid "steps = pass_diff(func, tilelang.transform.ThreadSync(\"shared\"))\n"
msgstr ""

